"""RHEL OS-only, two-phase, same-account EC2 upgrade performance reporting.

Phase 1: RHEL 8.8 baseline (default 15-day CloudWatch window).
Phase 2: post-final-upgrade RHEL 9.6 (from each host's supplied Sydney completion time).
Phase 2 also creates final-summary.html comparing the two phases.
Every phase creates HTML, CSV export controls, a status JSON and internal state JSON.

Upgrade completion timestamps are entered in Australia/Sydney local time. ZoneInfo
resolves AEDT/AEST from the calendar date; UTC is stored internally for CloudWatch.
No reboot-time guess is used because a reboot is not proof of an OS upgrade.

Python 3.12/3.13 AWS Lambda. Dependency: boto3 (included in AWS Lambda runtime).
Required environment variables: REPORT_BUCKET, REPORT_PREFIX, KMS_KEY_ARN.
Optional: CW_AGENT_NAMESPACE=CWAgent, SSM_WAIT_SECONDS=100, BASELINE_DAYS=15,
MAX_HOSTS=20, MAX_DISCOVERED_SERVICES=80.

Phase 1 event: hostnames + server_types (app/db).
Phase 2 event: same batch_id + upgrade_completed_at_sydney mapping for every hostname.

Non-core systemd services are auto-discovered in Phase 1 and compared after upgrade.
Historical CWAgent memory/disk/swap metrics must have been collected in advance.
SSM OS snapshots are live readings at each run, not retrospective history.
"""

